KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp14
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ function: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ lambda: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.spec.auto.general]/10, [expr.rel]/2, [expr.eq]/1: `return true;'
and `return st == 0;' both deduce bool.  The front end deduces the
comparison as __CPROVER_bool and rejects the function ("inconsistent
deduction for the return type: 'bool' and '__CPROVER_bool'").  libc++'s
__stop_state::__add_callback has such a lambda, so its body is dropped
(__stop_token/stop_state.h:140, for <stop_token>, <thread>, <future> and
<condition_variable>).  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept
this program (-std=c++14), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
